sacre for  example or something like that and try  to remake that because why that is just  pointless I feel like it's pointless and  they're just doing it as a cash grab and  it's just stupid and it's never going to  be as good you're  we're gonna capture that same atmosphere  particularly from horror movies of the  70s have a very particular style a very  particular aesthetic and you can't redo  that so as I said there's been rumors  going around that Suspiria was going to  be remade now initially the guy that was  supposed to direct it was named David  Gordon Green and I guess the production  kind of went round and round and there  were legal issues and stuff like that  and around 2013-2014 he said I don't  think it's ever gonna get made now and  everything like that and you know all  cult horror fans around the world  breathed a sigh of relief however just a  couple of years ago it was announced  that the remake was actually going  through it's going to be a different  director an Italian director named Luca  Guadagnino I hope I pronounced that  right he announced at the 72nd Venice  Film Festival that he was going to  direct the remake Tilda Swinton is gonna  be in it Dakota Johnson is gonna be in  it possibly ray Fiennes I do not know  how I feel about it I don't really want  to [ __ ] on something I haven't seen but  I just really do not think this is a  good idea one promising sign is that  he's going to set the movie in 1977 when  the original movie came out and he's  going to set it in Berlin the original  was actually set in Munich so it might  be alright in that sense but I've also  heard that it's not going to have the  visual look of the original so to me  again that seems pointless because the  thing about Suspiria is that it's whole  thing is its atmosphere its colors the  visual style of it that you know the  soundtrack everything like that  all of it goes together and I don't  think that the movie can be separated  from those aspects it's not so in a way  I think it's a movie that really can't  be remade because if you do it exactly  like the old one then that is also  pointless because we already have the  old one so why we do it just the same  but if you're going to remake it without  those crazy lights and those crazy  colors and just those you know those  gorgeous like grotesque murder scenes  and stuff like that if you're going to  make it without that then it's not  Suspiria anymore you know what I mean so  me it just seems like a pointless  exercise it's like if they want to make  a movie about a witch's coven just write  a different one I mean it could be  similar it could be inspired by but if  you're not gonna make it look like  Suspiria then it's not Suspiria and if  you do make it look like Suspiria then  you're just treading over ground that's  already been done so I really don't  think that there's any reason for it to  be remade and I really wish they  wouldn't have done it but evidently the  principal photography it has been filmed  apparently it was actually finished last  year last March but I don't know when  it's going to be released last I heard  that like I said the filming had been  finished  Jessica Harper does have a part in it so  she's not not in the same role she's not  reprising the role obviously but um she  has like some kind of cameo or something  like that in it which you know that's  cool I love her and stuff like that but  I don't know I just think the whole  thing is it is a bad idea I will  probably see it even though after I say  it I'm sure I wish I hadn't seen it  because I just I don't know I don't know  how it could be good even if it's good  it will still piss me off because you  know why didn't they just make another  witch movie and stuff like that but you  know whatever like I said I haven't seen  it so I can't super [ __ ] on it yet but I  just I think it's a stupid idea from the  get-go and I just really wish they  hadn't done it but I guess it's too late  now so anyway um if you were a horror  fan and you haven't already seen this  which would shock me if you hadn't but  maybe like a lot of younger people  haven't seen it because I know how how  that goes you know most of the movies  from the 70s and stuff like that maybe  so like people younger people that came  up with horror movies haven't got around  to seeing all the old ones yet like I  said if you're into gritty  straightforward type of horror or you  know stuff that's like plot focused or  character focused or something like that  then you might find this a little  strange because like I said it's more of  an experience you just kind of have to  you know sit back and let it wash over  you'll all these you know these  beautiful visuals and stuff like that it  is very creepy it does have some very  creepy scenes particularly the ones with  Helena Markos because she's got this  creepy voice and this creepy snore and  all this other kind of stuff but it's  you know it's really a classic classic  horror movie for a reason and if you  haven't seen it I would definitely  recommend it as I said the two  subsequent movies inferno I would  definitely  recommend mother of tears and you don't  really have to see it I didn't think it  was that great like I said I'd have to  see it again cuz it's probably been  eight or nine years since I've seen it  and I just I remember not liking it but  seriously check it out if you haven't  already as one of my favorite movies  ever definitely one of my favorite  horror movies and that will do it for  this hopefully last movie review that is  Tom 'less he should be back the evening  that this comes out so hopefully that  will go okay I know I said that last  time but hopefully for real this time  but if you like the show remember to  Like share subscribe on all your social  media if you would like to support the  show with a small donation then you can  go to our patreon page which is  patreon.com slash 13 o'clock podcast or  if you don't 